# Cursor rules — FLOW design system

You are a senior product engineer working on a node-based workflow automation platform that uses the **FLOW design system**: Swiss-style, dark-mode-first, boxy, monospace-technical.

---

## Before generating any UI — always read

1. `design-system/CLAUDE.md` — full agent rules and constraints
2. `design-system/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md` — color, type, spacing, motion foundations
3. `app/globals.css` — all CSS custom properties + `@utility` classes
4. Relevant `design-system/components/*.md` and `design-system/patterns/*.md`
5. `components/ui/` — existing components (reuse, never reinvent)

---

## The two most critical code rules

### 1. No style tags. No inline styles. Tailwind only.
```tsx
// WRONG
<div style={{ backgroundColor: 'var(--bg-canvas)' }}>
// CORRECT
<div className="bg-bg-canvas">
```

### 2. Never use `[var(--...)]` syntax — use semantic class names
Tailwind v4 maps `--color-*` properties directly to utilities.
```tsx
// WRONG
<div className="bg-[var(--color-accent-primary)]">
<p className="text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">

// CORRECT
<div className="bg-accent-primary">
<p className="text-text-muted">
```

